CafeFlow table games include rule modules from GameNest v2.2.0
(https://github.com/absswds/GameNest), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The JavaScript files under `upstream/games/` (game rules, their question/word
data files, `games/lib` helpers and `games/vendor`) are copied verbatim from
that project. The Persian catalogue, the seat/room layer, the WebSocket
protocol and every screen are CafeFlow's own work; GameNest's server, page
shell renderers and language packs are not used. One rule helper lives outside
`games/` upstream: `public/js/paodekuai-patterns.js`, vendored unchanged at
`upstream/public/js/` because the paodekuai module requires it.

The full Apache-2.0 text is in `LICENSE` next to this file.

This product includes software developed by Jeff Hlywa (https://github.com/jhlywa/chess.js)
- chess.js v0.12.1, BSD-2-Clause, vendored at games/vendor/chessjs.js


matter-js 0.19.0 (MIT) is bundled in public/vendor/ for the Suika battle game.

games/lib/zh-variants.js contains a Traditional-to-Simplified Chinese character table generated
from OpenCC (https://github.com/BYVoid/OpenCC, Apache-2.0) via opencc-js 1.0.5.
